      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Salt water"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "An ordinary shark with a streamlined body, narrow snout, prominent dorsal fin, and forked tail. The Fish entry gives no separate size or color for this row."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Hit Dice variants mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "3 HD · THAC0 17, bite 2–5, 65 XP.",
            "4 HD · THAC0 17, bite 2–5, 120 XP.",
            "5 HD · THAC0 15, bite 2–8, 175 XP.",
            "6 HD · THAC0 15, bite 2–8, 270 XP.",
            "7 HD · THAC0 13, bite 3–12, 420 XP.",
            "8 HD · THAC0 13, bite 3–12, 650 XP."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Combat mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Feeding frenzy · A shark can detect the scent of blood a mile away. The scent of blood and a kill can excite sharks into a feeding frenzy.",
            "Bite and retreat · Sharks close in, bite, and retreat. Up to ten normal-sized sharks can attack one man-sized opponent this way."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "3–12 appearing. Average (10) morale.",
            "The Salt Water summoning tables list sharks at 3–5, 5–6, and 7–8 HD.",
            "Monstrous Manual, TSR 2140, January 1994 third printing, Fish pp. 117–118, with saltwater summoning on p. 378."
          ]
        }
      ],
