      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Salt water"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A huge prehistoric-style shark, named megalodon in the entry. The portrait gives it a thick torso and broad jaws. The entry gives no measured length or color."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Hit Dice variants mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "10 HD · THAC0 11, bite 4–16, 2,000 XP.",
            "11 HD · THAC0 9, bite 4–16, 3,000 XP.",
            "12 HD · THAC0 9, bite 5–20, 5,000 XP.",
            "13 HD · THAC0 7, bite 5–20, 6,000 XP.",
            "14 HD · THAC0 7, bite 6–24, 7,000 XP.",
            "15 HD · THAC0 5, bite 6–24, 8,000 XP."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Combat mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Swallow whole · A Giant Shark can swallow most creatures whole when the attack roll is 4 above the minimum needed to hit. The entry says Giant Sharks never enter a feeding frenzy."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Shared Fish rules mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Digestion and suffocation · A swallowed creature takes normal bite damage, then 1 point of digestion damage per round and a 5% cumulative chance of suffocating per round.",
            "Escape · A victim can cut free with a sharp-edged weapon. Others can cut or tear from the outside. The victim breaks free when the fish has lost 50% of its hit points."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "1–3 appearing. Steady (11) morale.",
            "Monster Summoning VIII lists the Giant Shark in the Salt Water table.",
            "Monstrous Manual, TSR 2140, January 1994 third printing, Fish pp. 117–118, with saltwater summoning on p. 378."
          ]
        }
      ],
